Yashichi wrote:
>
> If I read correctly, alignments are adjusted only if the artifact is given
> by a god, not if wished for; thus a wish for magicbane will produce a
> neutral-aligned artifact no matter who wishes for it.

They are modified at the start of the game based on your class and
alignment.  For a lawful Valk, Mojo and the Orb of Fate are lawfull.
For each class that has a guaranteed first gift, that artifact gets
modified at the start of the game.  For each character its class's
quest artifact gets modified at the start of the game.  It is not
done at gift time.

> It's impossible to
> wish for an alignment on an artifact, e.g. "blessed chaotic magicbane,"
> correct? Or is it possible to adjust the alignment on a non-intelligent
> artifact by wishing?

Correct and it is not possible.

> If all co-aligned and unaligned artifacts already exist in the game, will
> a god start drawing gifts from other alignments (subject to the lengthy
> 2/n+1 odds), and will those alignments be adjusted? Or will ze just "run
> out" of available gifts?

They run out.  Gifts *only* come from 1) the guaranteed first gift if
your class has one, adjusted to your alignment at the start of the game,
2) other artifacts of your alignment, 3) unaligned artifacts.

You can only get cross-aligned artifacts by means other than gifts.
Two can be named.  Certain monsters can get two others.  Any weapon
found on the floor has a chance of being an artifact of any alignment
including cross-aligned.  In the planes player monsters get artifact
weapons and if you have all of the co-aligned and unaligned ones only
cross-aligned ones are left.

But you CAN change alignments and be able to get gifts from other
dieties.  Permanent or temporary alignment changes are both possible.
Once you've gotten many artifacts it tends to be not worth the time
it takes unless you're playing an extinctionist character.

